# The event model of one grounded action.
#
# This is what a PDDL action's preconditions and effects cannot express, and so
# what `get domain action details` on the classical terminal cannot show: an
# action here is a set of events, each with its own precondition and effects,
# plus a statement per agent of which events that agent can tell apart. That
# last part is what makes an action informative rather than merely effective.

# The grounded action name, as `get_epistemic_domain` lists it.
string action
---
bool success
string error

# Every event of the model, by name.
string[] events

# The designated events: the ones that can actually occur. One means the action
# is ontic and its outcome is settled by the action alone. More than one means
# it is sensing, and which occurred has to be observed.
string[] designated_events

# The precondition of each event, as a formula in the domain's vocabulary, in
# the same order as `events`. Empty means the event has none.
string[] preconditions

# The effects of each event, in the same order: a rendering of which atoms it
# makes true and which false, and under what condition.
string[] effects

# One line per agent, in the order `get_epistemic_domain` lists them, saying
# what that agent observes of this action. This is the part with no PDDL
# counterpart: two agents can be equally affected by an action and learn
# entirely different things from it.
string[] observability
